codex
The failure is now localized to Lean’s startup call to `readlink("/proc/<pid>/exe")`; that call is denied in this sandbox even though the pinned binary and libraries are present. I’m applying a narrow audit-only preload shim that supplies the process’s own `argv[0]` only when that exact self-executable lookup fails. It does not alter Lean sources, generated sources, proof terms, or compiler behavior.
apply patch
patch: completed
